# Fixture files stay in, whatever a contributor's global excludes drop:
# `**/.claude/settings.local.json` and other dotfiles Agents use. The repo's
# rules beat `core.excludesFile`, and later rules here beat these, so build
# output stays ignored even inside a fixture. The folders that hold the
# fixtures are re-included too: git skips the files of an ignored folder.
# `cargo xtask fixtures` fails when git ignores a fixture file.
!crates/*/tests/
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/**

.claude/worktrees/
target/
node_modules/
crates/config-digger-app/gen/
crates/config-digger-app/ui/dist/
crates/config-digger-app/permissions/autogenerated/
crates/config-digger-app/ui/screenshots/
